%S A399498 0,0,0,0,4,16,43,134,425,1229,3450,9625,26467,71570,191814,509083,
%T A399498 1340678,3504391,9103909,23517452,60431603,154608247,393755587,
%U A399498 999333185,2526164978,6367872760,15995302728,40085909835,100142920787,249700259569,620847470396
%N A399498 Number of equivalence classes under rotations and reflections of n-step self-avoiding walks on the square lattice that use both coordinate axes and have exactly 2 pairs of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%C A399498 In the notation of Nemirovsky et al. (1992), a(n) = p_{n,2}^{(2)}.
%C A399498 Translations are removed by fixing the initial vertex at the origin. The full 8-element square-lattice point group acts on the ordered vertex sequence; path reversal is not included in the equivalence relation.
%C A399498 The values through n=11 appear in Table II, p. 1093, of Nemirovsky et al. (1992). The values through n=59 are obtained from A033323, whose exact terms through 59 come from the ancillary file sq_isaw_counts.ser accompanying Beaton, Guttmann, and Jensen (2020).
%H A399498 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A399498/b399498.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..59</a>
%H A399498 N. R. Beaton, A. J. Guttmann, and I. Jensen, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.05852">Two-dimensional interacting self-avoiding walks: new estimates for critical temperatures and exponents</a>, arXiv:1911.05852 [cond-mat.stat-mech], 2020.
%H A399498 A. M. Nemirovsky, K. F. Freed, T. Ishinabe, and J. F. Douglas, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01049010">Marriage of exact enumeration and 1/d expansion methods: lattice model of dilute polymers</a>, J. Statist. Phys. 67 (1992), 1083-1108; see Eq. 5 (p. 1090), Eq. 7b (p. 1093), and Table II (p. 1093).
%F A399498 a(n) = A033323(n)/8.
%e A399498 a(5) = 4. One representative has successive vertices v_0 = (0,0), v_1 = (1,0), v_2 = (1,1), v_3 = (0,1), v_4 = (0,2), v_5 = (1,2). Its two contacts are {v_0,v_3} and {v_2,v_5}.
%Y A399498 Cf. A033323 (corresponding rooted square-lattice walks), A038747 (companion coefficient p_{n,1}^{(2)}), A049230 (d=3, m=2 total), A046788 (d=4, m=2 total), A038728 (d=5, m=2 total).
%K A399498 nonn,walk,new
%O A399498 1,5
%A A399498 _Carlo Corti_, Aug 30 2026
